00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:03.889 align:start position:0%
here's a nice logic puzzle from  shakuntala Devi a family has several  children each boy in the family has as  many sisters as brothers but each of the  girls has twice as many brothers as  sisters how many boys and girls are  there  to work it out let's say the number of  boys is equal to B and the number of  girls is equal to G for each of the boys  each boy will have B minus one brothers  because you don't want to count the boy  himself then each boy will have G  sisters similarly each girl has B  brothers and G minus one sisters now  each boy has as many sisters as brothers  that means that B minus one is equal to  G  now each of the girls has twice as many  brothers as sisters that means that b is  equal to 2 multiplied by G minus one we  now solve this system of equations we  can substitute in so that we get 2  multiplied by G minus 1 minus one is  equal to G so that 2G minus three is  equal to G then G is equal to 3 and  since B minus 1 is equal to g b is equal  to four there are three girls and four  boys
 

